---
layout: layouts/piece.njk
title: "The Café — Closed Post (1080 × 1350)"
canvasW: "1080px"
canvasH: "1350px"
pageCss: "/assets/css/studio/fb-closed.css"

# Which entry of site.json's closedDays this post is for. The holiday, the
# day back and the thank-you are there, shared with the door sign
# (sign-closed-bw), and the caption (fb-closed.11tydata.js) reads the same
# entry, so the picture and the words can't disagree. For another holiday,
# add its entry, change this date, and reword the studio lines below.
closedDate: "2026-11-11"

tags: studio
studioWeekly: true
studioTitle: "Closed for Veterans Day — Facebook post"
studioCategory: "Social"
studioSize: "1080 × 1350 px · portrait feed post"
studioNote: "Closed Wednesday, November 11 for Veterans Day, back Thursday, November 12 (client 2026-10-31). The holiday is the biggest thing on it and the week is shown open or closed, so it can't be read as the cafe closing. Post Monday, November 9; once the day has passed, edit the post to start 'Outdated. Thank You' like the weekly posts. Reads closedDays in site.json."
studioW: 1080
studioH: 1350
studioOrder: 25
---
{#- The holiday first, then the day, then the week around it.

    THE HOLIDAY IS THE BIGGEST THING ON IT (client 2026-10-31): with "We're
    closed" as the headline, a quick look says the cafe is closed, not that
    it's one day off. THE WEEK under it shows every other day open.

    A cream body between the teal bands, so the red can be read (never red on
    teal). The red, teal and cream with the stars are all the holiday styling
    it needs: no flag, no emoji.

    Every size is set for the ~540px a portrait post shows at on a phone:
    nothing a customer needs is under 24px. -#}
{%- set c = (site.closedDays | where("date", closedDate))[0] %}
{%- set o = site.opening %}
{%- set opens = (o.opens.time | replace(":00", "")) + o.opens.meridiem %}
{%- set closes = (o.closes.time | replace(":00", "")) + o.closes.meridiem %}
{%- set star = "50,2 60.8,35.2 95.6,35.2 67.4,55.7 78.2,88.8 50,68.3 21.8,88.8 32.6,55.7 4.4,35.2 39.2,35.2" %}
<div class="canvas fc">

    <header class="fc-head">
        <div class="wordmark wordmark--light wordmark--hero fc-wordmark">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>
        <p class="p-display-italic fc-kicker">Holiday Hours</p>
        <p class="p-label fc-range">{{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="fc-body">
        <p class="p-display-italic fc-for">Closed for</p>
        <h1 class="p-display fc-holiday">{{ c.name }}</h1>
        <p class="p-display fc-date">{{ c.date | dayDate("long") }}</p>

        {% include "partials/studio/closed-week.njk" %}

        <div class="fc-stars" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- for size in ["side", "mid", "side"] %}
            <svg class="fc-star fc-star--{{ size }}" viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><polygon points="{{ star }}"/></svg>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>

        {%- if c.thanks %}
        <p class="p-display-italic fc-thanks">{{ c.thanks }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>

    <footer class="fc-foot">
        <p class="p-display fc-foot-call">{{ site.phone }} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ site.social.website }}</p>
        <p class="p-body fc-foot-line">{{ o.hoursDays }}, {{ opens }} &ndash; {{ closes }} &middot; {{ site.address.street }}, {{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </footer>

</div>
